<title>JAPAN: Japan trade surplus jumps 69.7 percent in July.</title>
<headline>Japan trade surplus jumps 69.7 percent in July.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's customs-cleared trade surplus recorded another hefty jump in July, rising 69.7 percent from a year earlier, the Ministry of Finance said on Monday.</p>
<p>The overall surplus came in at 849.08 billion yen, while the surplus with the United States grew 35.7 percent to 420.55 billion yen.</p>
